Chapter: TextOrderAllowed
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 Second, `text-compare` is the encoding order and stays. It orders by CCE
 code point, which is NOT the alphabet: 'd' is 22 and 'b' is 32, so d sorts
 before b. That is correct for a data structure and wrong for a column a
 human reads, which is why the two orders have different names.

Section: Helpers

  b2i : Boolean -> Integer
  b2i (b) = if b then 1 else 0

  mk : Integer -> Text
  mk (n) = char-to-text (code-to-char n)

  sign : Integer -> Integer
  sign (n) = if n < 0 then (0 - 1) else if n > 0 then 1 else 0

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni ("eq-same-content = " & show (b2i (mk 15 == mk 15)))
    print-line-uni ("eq-diff-content = " & show (b2i (mk 15 == mk 32)))
    print-line-uni ("neq-diff        = " & show (b2i (mk 15 /= mk 32)))
    print-line-uni ("cmp-a-b         = " & show (sign (text-compare "a" "b")))
    print-line-uni ("cmp-a-a         = " & show (sign (text-compare "a" "a")))
    print-line-uni ("cmp-d-b         = " & show (sign (text-compare "d" "b")))
  end

